WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.620
Apple’s 2018 iPad Pro is revolutionary in
the iPad world, but it also came with a few

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:13.219
drawbacks like the $800 price tag, no headphone
jack, bendgate issues, and worst of all, the

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:18.910
incredibly powerful A12X processor and the
new USB-C port are way ahead of what the current

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.609
iOS software allows you to do with it.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:26.169
But what if there was an iPad that maybe wasn’t
as nice as the Pro, but solved a lot of these

00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:27.220
problems?

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.289
Could it be Apple’s brand new 2019 iPad
Air?

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:31.500
Let’s find out!

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.350
For starters, it comes with a headphone jack,
you won’t have any bending issues, it’s

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:42.130
packing the same new 7nm A12 processor from
the iPhone XS, and it’s priced at a whopping

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.680
$300 cheaper than the Pro.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.010
Even better, you don’t have a buy a new
Apple Pencil if you already have the old one.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.320
So that’s it, right?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.469
People should obviously just by the new Air?

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:54.170
Well, not quite.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.160
The Pro’s got some tricks up its sleeve.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.899
The new square-edged design makes it look
futuristic and modern compared to the Air,

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:04.690
but it’s not as comfortable to hold compared
to the old design.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.280
The Pro gets Face ID instead of Touch ID,
which works great by the way since there’s

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.970
no visible notch and it works in literally
any orientation, even upside down.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:19.830
Thanks to Face ID, there’s even bezels,
all around, with rounded corners on the display,

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:24.080
which really makes it stand out from the crowd
and it actually makes it easier to play games

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.369
in landscape mode.

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:30.229
Now the display tech is extremely similar,
there are literally only 2 differences.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:33.450
The Pro is brighter and it gets ProMotion
technology.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.740
Testing the brightness, you can see the difference,
but does it actually matter much in the real

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:38.740
world?

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.240
Honestly, not that much.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.530
Now ProMotion, on the other hand, is huge
in my book.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:48.651
It allows the screen to refresh at up to 120hz
for buttery smooth navigation, and you truly

00:01:48.651 --> 00:01:50.570
can feel the difference.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:54.840
Now what people don’t mention about ProMotion
is that it automatically brings down the refresh

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.710
rate to match the content you’re viewing
to help save battery life.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:03.540
So let’s say you’re watching a video that’s
shot at 24 frames per second, like this one,

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.720
the Pro will run at 24hz while the Air runs
at 60hz, wasting battery life without giving

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.880
any visible benefit at all.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.830
Another benefit of ProMotion is reduced Apple
Pencil lag, and as you can see in this slow-mo

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:20.770
clip, drawing on the Pro is almost instant,
and it’s a difference you can feel.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.320
Speaking of the Pencil, the Pro supports the
new one, which is better in basically every

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.270
way, especially in the way it magnetically
connects to the side, instantly pairs and

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.860
wirelessly charges.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.660
The matte design feels better in the hand
and it’s got a new double-tap to switch

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.580
tools feature which is incredibly useful.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.270
Something that’s a much bigger deal than
people make it out to be is that the Pro gets

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.580
4 speakers instead of 2 on the Air.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.720
It truly makes a world of a difference.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.400
You get true stereo sound in landscape mode,
which makes a huge difference for gaming.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.331
Let’s listen to a quick speaker comparison,
and make sure you put in some headphones so

00:02:55.331 --> 00:03:04.440
you can hear the difference.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:15.450
Yep, the speakers are many times better on
the Pro.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.370
The interesting thing about the new Air is
that it’s the only non-Pro iPad that has

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.400
a smart connector and supports the smart keyboard.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.590
Before we get into performance, let’s quickly
mention the camera differences, even though

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.950
cameras don’t matter much on iPads.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:34.290
The Pro gets more megapixels on the rear for
better photos with Smart HDR and 4K video

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.950
recording at 60 frames per second.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.860
Unlike the Air, it gets quad-LED flash.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:44.480
The front-facing camera isn’t much different,
but thanks to it having Face ID, you can take

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.930
portrait selfies which really does make a
big difference.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:04:01.230
The Pro also packs 5 microphones instead of
only 2 on the Air, so let’s compare them.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:06.260
Getting into performance, the Pro gets the
A12X chip while the Air gets the A12.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:11.900
And yes, you can play Fortnite and other titles
at 60 frames per second on both of these iPads.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.210
The Pro gets 4GB of RAM compared to 3 on the
Air.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:20.680
Yes, you can get 6GB on the Pro if you buy
the 1TB model but it’s definitely not worth

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.730
the price for almost everyone.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:29.510
In Geekbench 4, the Pro is only 4.5% faster
in single core, and a much higher 59% faster

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:32.230
in multi-core, which is what really matters.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:36.900
In the metal graphics test, the Pro scored
over twice as high as the Air, which is gonna

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.690
be huge for things like gaming, rendering
and augmented reality.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:46.100
The more realistic Antutu test that takes
the processor, graphics, RAM and user experience

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:50.390
into account only shows a 47% improvement
for the Pro.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:56.990
For an even more realistic test, we exported
the same 4K HEVC 60p video file on both iPads,

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:01.380
and the Pro was finished in less than half
the time, now that’s a significant difference

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.570
for video editings.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:07.260
So as we can see, there’s a pretty big difference
in performance, but will you notice that difference

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.610
in day-to-day use?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:13.110
Let’s play Fortnite, which is one of the
most graphically intensive games on iOS, and

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.280
see if there are any differences.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.720
Playing Fortnite, the iPad Air runs the game
perfectly at 60 frames per second on high

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:19.720
settings.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:23.660
After playing for a while, it’s incredibly
smooth with no dropped frames at all.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:28.110
I honestly couldn’t tell the difference
between it and the Pro in terms of game smoothness

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.550
and graphics quality.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.330
The biggest noticeable difference was only
having 2 speakers on the Air.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:38.690
So for gaming, the iPad Air can handle basically
any popular game currently available on iOS,

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:42.960
so the extra power of the iPad Pro isn’t
really being used unless you’re one of the

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.400
few people who is actually going to do something
like video editing.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.150
In basic navigation and just using the iPads
daily, you’ll definitely notice a difference

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:56.560
with the Pro, but it’s not due to performance,
it’s due to the ProMotion tech.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.750
You can easily feel the difference in display
smoothness with the iPad Pro, and that’s

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.160
what you’ll feel every day.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.270
The quad-speaker setup is also a difference
you’ll feel every day, maybe even more so

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:07.270
than ProMotion.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:08.710
So what’s the rundown?

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.510
Which iPad is the better value?

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:15.760
Well, the iPad Pro is obviously ahead of its
time, since the hardware is all there but

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.560
it’s limited by iOS.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:21.460
If you’re planning to keep it for many years,
the software will eventually catch up and

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.380
you might actually be able to use all of that
power.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.780
Some people will buy the iPad Pro just for
new modern design alone.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.100
It’s definitely a much better iPad, but
it’s also quite a bit more expensive.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:37.180
Now the new iPad Air honestly has enough performance
for almost everyone and the display quality

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.410
is outstanding.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.490
It supports the Apple pencil, the smart keyboard,
and it has a headphone jack.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:46.340
It’s basically the best all-around iPad
currently available if you’re not looking

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:50.880
to spend close to a thousand dollars, but
it’s got a couple of compromises, no ProMotion,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.639
and only 2 speakers.

00:06:52.639 --> 00:06:57.310
Now what if you could spend that same $500,
or even less, and get basically everything

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.750
the iPad Air gets, but with 4 speakers and
ProMotion technology as well?

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:07.160
That’s basically what you get with the 2017
10.5” iPad Pro, which is currently on sale

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.960
on Amazon brand-new for $500.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:17.970
The A10X chip is not much slower in processor
performance and it’s actually almost 50%

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.770
faster in graphics performance.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:25.470
It even supports 60 fps on Fortnite and runs
it just as smooth as on the new iPad Air.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:31.200
People say the A10X will stop being supported
sooner, but the iPad Mini 2 from 2013 still

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:36.900
supports iOS 12, so the 2017 iPad Pro should
still be supported for at least another 5

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:41.950
years, and by the time it loses support, you’ll
honestly be okay with it, since you enjoyed

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:46.240
the much better speakers, ProMotion technology
and better graphics performance for all of

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.240
those years.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.670
If you enjoyed this comparison video, make
sure to hit that subscribe button because

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.660
we’ve got a lot more video comparisons like
this one coming, including videos on the new

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.660
2019 iMac.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.669
This has been Vadim from Max Tech, thanks
for watching, and we’ll see you in the next

00:07:59.669 --> 00:08:02.949
one.

